  "term": "vestibular receptors",
  "definition": "Vestibular receptors are the developing sensory structures of the ear that were examined as one of the sensory organs in this mouse embryo gene-expression study. In this context, they are treated as part of the vestibular, or balance-related, sensory epithelium of the developing ear.",
